        ["During the history, a 64-year-old reports 15 pounds of unintentional weight loss over 2 months and back pain that wakes him every night regardless of position. How should you interpret this?",["Red flags that need physician referral","Typical findings of mechanical back pain","Signs that he needs harder exercise","Irrelevant to the musculoskeletal exam"],"Unexplained weight loss and constant night pain unchanged by position are classic red flags for malignancy or infection."],
        ["Which step of the management model involves making clinical judgments based on the data gathered during the examination?",["Evaluation","Examination","Intervention","Outcomes"],"Evaluation is the dynamic process of interpreting examination findings, which leads to the diagnosis and prognosis."],
        ["A patient lives alone in a second-floor apartment with no elevator. In the ICF model, this information is best classified as what?",["An environmental factor","A body structure impairment","A participation restriction","An activity limitation"],"Physical surroundings, social supports, and attitudes are environmental factors that can help or hinder function."],
        ["A runner's pain worsens with prolonged sitting, eases with walking, and does not wake her at night. How does this pattern MOST influence your hypothesis?",["It suggests a mechanical problem suited to PT management","It strongly suggests a visceral cause requiring referral","It confirms a malignancy that needs urgent imaging","It means the history is not useful for the diagnosis"],"Symptoms that change predictably with posture and activity behave mechanically. Constant pain unaffected by position or rest raises concern for non-musculoskeletal causes."],
        ["Which statement belongs in the Assessment section of a SOAP note?",["Limited knee flexion and quad weakness limit stair climbing","Patient states her knee hurts most on stairs","Knee flexion AROM 95 degrees, quad strength 4-/5","Continue quad sets and progress step-ups next visit"],"The Assessment interprets the findings and links impairments to function. The other options are subjective, objective, and plan statements."],
        ["During the systems review, you notice a non-blanching red area over the sacrum of a patient referred for knee rehab. Which system is this screen part of?",["Integumentary","Neuromuscular","Musculoskeletal","Cardiopulmonary"],"Skin integrity, color, and scars are part of the integumentary screen. A non-blanching area suggests a pressure injury that needs attention even though it is outside the referral area."],
        ["A 40-year-old reports shoulder pain, but also mentions fatigue, night sweats, and unintended weight loss. What is the MOST appropriate next step?",["Complete the exam and refer to the physician for medical screening","Treat the shoulder for 6 weeks and refer if it has not improved","Ignore the systemic complaints, since they are not musculoskeletal","Begin aggressive shoulder mobilization to settle the pain"],"Constitutional symptoms such as night sweats, fatigue, and weight loss are red flags for systemic disease. Document and refer while noting your musculoskeletal findings."],
        ["Which element of the management model includes the plan of care and the predicted time to reach goals?",["Prognosis","Diagnosis","Examination","Outcomes"],"In the APTA model, the prognosis states the expected level of improvement and the time needed, and it includes the plan of care."]
